From 16c86ed895f7f659882056a86d07ec8b4f4c16c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 11:15:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Collapse the two drag settings into one Invert switch

"Map drag" (Orig / 1:1) and "Invert" (Yes / No) were two switches over
one bit. Viewport.handle_event already divides the drag delta by the zoom
with a carry, and move_by_pixels does no scaling of its own, so the only
thing "Orig" vs "1:1" ever changed was the sign that handle_drag applies
- exactly what Invert changed. Four combinations, two behaviours:

    sign +1  ==  Orig  ==  1:1 + invert
    sign -1  ==  Orig + invert  ==  1:1

So the Map drag row is gone and Invert takes its place at y 110, keeping
the known-good clickmap row (x 88..128, y 106..122) that lines up with
the value drawn at column 11. Default is Invert = No, which is the old
"1:1": the map travels with the pointer and the pixel under the cursor
stays under it. Yes gives Freeserf's original direction.

global.map_drag_1to1 and Action.options_map_invert are removed;
Action.options_map_drag is kept so the rest of the enum does not
renumber. The arrow keys still scroll the way they point either way.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DFktm5o1kLnS2Pgvyp8tD4
